## Facts
- Java fix and rationale: commit `ed156f5983` (`git show ed156f5983`): the offer row/deadline (900 ms
  courier decision timeout) was recorded BEFORE awaiting the Tracking status publish, so a slow
  publish consumed the courier's response window, contrary to the sample contract §7.2
  (`framework/doc/framework/common/sample/deliverydispatch/README.ko.md:292-296`: the attempt expires
  only when courier A does not answer within the deadline AFTER receiving the offer). The java fix
  creates the offer row inside the publish completion, immediately followed by the one-way courier
  send, first dispatch and re-dispatch alike; regression test DispatchWorkerDeadlineTest.
- The other three implementations still record the deadline before the publish
  (`bucketB-java-deliverydispatch-summary.md` parity section):
  cpp `framework/languages/cpp/samples/DeliveryDispatch/Server/Dispatch/main.cpp:205-207,243-246`;
  dotnet `framework/languages/dotnet/samples/DeliveryDispatch/Server/Dispatch/DispatchWorker.cs:138-141,200-203`;
  node `framework/languages/node/samples/DeliveryDispatch.Ts/Server/DispatchCenter/dispatch-worker.ts:63-83`.
  They currently pass by timing; make them match the contract and java.
- Env: cpp `ZLINK_CPP_BUILD_DIR=/home/hep7/project/zlink/framework/languages/cpp/build/linux-ninja-c-e2e`
